creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8859310Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8869853Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8978164Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8990222Z ^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8990983Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8991515Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8991728Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8991997Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8993269Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8993674Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8993926Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8994501Z    if you are ready to continue.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8994777Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8995720Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8996587Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8997280Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8997798Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8998038Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8998276Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8998657Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8998961Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8999510Z    can use Nix.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8999773Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.8999909Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9000166Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9000595Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9001285Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9006256Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9006692Z I will:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9006987Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9007268Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9007869Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9008483Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9008981Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9009255Z  - install Nix in /nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9009518Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9009907Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9010328Z    /root
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9022614Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9023206Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9034837Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9035586Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9036285Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9037308Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9037812Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9057137Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9057806Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9069012Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9069660Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9070264Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9070564Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9070792Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9071180Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9071469Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9072095Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9072431Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9072579Z If you would like to
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9073011Z see the output, try like this:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9073379Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9073757Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9074436Z   $ sh ./install-nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9074583Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9074593Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9074828Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T16:07:07.9083581Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
